  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ensure respect for, promote and realize fundamental principles and rights at work</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. District-level governance structures in the Punjab province have been capacitated to address Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work (FPRW), such as the District Vigilance Committees to organize community-based campaigns to eliminate child labour, and the Child Protection Centres to rescue children and enroll them in the schools, as well as to support women&#x2019;s economic participation through their increased mobility, organizing, representation and access to finances. Other local community structures in the province, represented by relevant government institutions, social partners and civil society organizations, have started implementing, monitoring, and promoting actions around the elimination of child labour; elimination of forced labour; promotion of non-discrimination, gender equality, and social dialogue within the cotton supply chain. As a result, the number of children in formal schools has increased in the province, while two farmers associations and four trade unions in the agriculture sector have been organized. The formal registration of the farmer associations and trade unions is in process with the concerned authorities. A provincial tripartite task force was also established, which meets regularly to discuss the decent work deficits in the cotton supply chain. 
2. Employers Federation of Pakistan prepared a 5-year inclusive strategy to implement FPRW in the agriculture sector (specific to farmers) nationwide. In partnership with the EU and INDITEX, the ILO enhanced the capacity of the social partners, government, and governance structures at the community/district level to understand the integrated approach and pilot integrated (FPRW based) interventiosn in the cotton supply chain. The ILO provided a solid knowledge base to the stakeholders though mapping of the decent work deficits in the cotton supply chain.</narrative>
   </description>
